    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Henry Kee & Son are thrilled to present this pristine three-bedroom bungalow, nestled in one of Donegal's most breathtaking coastal settings on approx. 1.18 acres of exquisite landscaped gardens. The bright, expansive interior is in absolute turn-key condition, featuring entrance porch, hallway, sitting room, kitchen/dining room, three bedrooms (main bedroom en-suite), and a main shower room. Spanning the entire first floor, the kitchen/dining area beautifully frames the panoramic sea and coastal scenery. The majestic grounds showcase immaculate lawns, sculpted rockeries, specimen trees, ornamental shrubs, a bespoke architectural stone feature and a sweeping gravel driveway. Offering total serenity and seclusion, these gardens form a spectacular vantage point to absorb the coastal scenery and crisp Atlantic air. Early viewing is essential to fully appreciate this coastal gem."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Parch, Sitting Room, Kitchen/Dining Room, Three Bedrooms (Main Bedroom with En-suite) and Shower Room.<br><br>\nEntrance Porch - 2.38m x 1.56m <br>Front door,\n2 No. Windows,\nTiled floor.<br><br><br>\nHallway - 3.39m x 1.77m <br>Pine flooring,\nStairs to lower ground floor and stairs up to kitchen/Dining room, \nRadiator.<br><br><br>\nSitting Room - 4.95m x 4.20m <br>Pine flooring‚\nTriple Aspect with 2 windows overlooking rockery to front‚ 1 gable window and French door overlooking the lawns‚\nOpen fire with feature stone surround and brace‚ Radiator & TV point.\nVaulted ceiling.<br><br><br>\nHallway - 1.06m x 2.15m <br>Carpeted, \nDoor opening to rear,\nAiring cupboard.<br><br><br>\nMain Bedroom - 3.67m x 3.05m <br>Carpeted,\nWall to wall fitted wardrobes,\nLarge window and door to rear with views of the garden and sea,\nRadiator.\n\nENSUITE: 2.07m x 1.76m\nWhite WHB, WC & Shower\nLaminate timber floor,\nWindow & radiator.<br><br><br>\nBedroom Two - 4.48m x 2.98m <br>Carpeted,\nFitted wardrobes, \nWindow to rear,\nRadiator.<br><br><br>\nBedroom Three - 2.81 m x 2.11m <br>Carpeted,\nWindow to rear,\nRadiator.<br><br><br>\nShower Room - 2.2m x 2.0m <br>White WHB, WC & Shower\nLaminate timber floor,\nWindow & radiator.<br><br><br>\nKitchen/Dining Room - 6.54m x3.07m <br>Pine flooring‚\nDouble doors leading to rear access steps - stunning sea & garden views‚\nVaulted ceiling with dual aspect, North & South facing, velux windows‚\nOpen fire with feature stone surround and brace‚\nHigh & low level units‚\nElectric Hob & Oven‚ Dishwasher & fridge.\nOpen fire with feature stone surround and chimney brace. <br><br>"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Extending to c. 1.18 acres the site is fully landscaped, completely enclosed by walls/fencing, and accessed via electric gates\nDunfanaghy town centre within walking distance, 0.5km approx.\nNearby attractions include Killahoey Blue Flag Beach, Dunfanaghy Gold Club, Portnablagh Pier & Harbour and the stunning Horn Head one of Donegal's most dramatic cliff viewpoints with panoramic Atlantic views (approx. 7km)\nSea views from property\nFeature stone rockery with sunken lawn named 'The Bear Pit'.\nSpacious patio area overlooking 'The Bear Pit', is a wonderful sun trap perfect for relaxing, entertaining and enjoying the views. \nLow maintenance gardens with stone-chip covered scrub beds and lawns\nLarge, bright and airy sitting room with high level ceiling and triple aspect windows\nWindows mostly triple glazed\nTwo open fires with feature stone chimney brace.\nOption to purchase some contents if desired."
      },
      {
